    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.04,
      "end_seconds": 201.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "okay, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.41,
      "end_seconds": 210.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Oh, I have thin bones, for two years. Well, I've had epilepsy, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.94,
      "end_seconds": 219.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "Right, right. Okay, I can see epilepsy in your file as well. Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.5,
      "end_seconds": 235.87,
      "duration_seconds": 15.37,
      "text": "So, um, I'm on alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week for my bones. Carbamazepine, 200 milligrams, twice a day for the seizures. I've been putting this off for weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.97,
      "end_seconds": 256.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.98,
      "end_seconds": 260.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Erm, not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.82,
      "end_seconds": 264.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.46,
      "end_seconds": 271.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "I, I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.52,
      "end_seconds": 275.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.09,
      "end_seconds": 279.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.36,
      "end_seconds": 282.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "and your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.4,
      "end_seconds": 288.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.89,
      "end_seconds": 296.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, it fits best with osteoporosis with a fragility fracture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.19,
      "end_seconds": 300.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Um, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.76,
      "end_seconds": 313.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.04,
      "text": "I understand the the worry. At the moment I'd say it's osteoporosis with a fragility fracture, and we'll know more once the blood tests is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.17,
      "end_seconds": 343.3,
      "duration_seconds": 14.13,
      "text": "let's get blood tests, for osteoporosis i'd rather check than guess, and and this is the quickest way to know more let's get a bone density scan, for osteoporosis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.86,
      "end_seconds": 346.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.42,
      "end_seconds": 370.64,
      "duration_seconds": 22.22,
      "text": "Take the tablet with a full glass of water, and stay upright for thirty minutes. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Come back in three months. Right, that's the plan. Do you wanna ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.04,
      "end_seconds": 379.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "let me think, uh, okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    },
